<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>How It Works – PickMates</title>
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css" />
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <div class="header-inner">
      <a href="/" class="logo"><span class="logo-flag">⛳⚽</span> PickMates</a>
      <nav><%- include('partials/nav') %></nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main>
    <div class="page-header">
      <h1>How It Works</h1>
      <p class="last-updated">The rules for all three game modes.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Golf Draft ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <h2 class="section-title" id="golf-draft">⛳ Golf Draft</h2>
    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:.8rem">
      <ol style="margin:0;padding-left:1.2rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.5rem">
        <li>Join a game and wait for the host to start the draft.</li>
        <li>The draft is a <strong>snake draft</strong> — players take turns picking real PGA Tour golfers, with the order reversing each round so it's fair (1→N, then N→1). Everyone drafts <strong><%= PICKS_PER_PLAYER %></strong> golfers.</li>
        <li>Your <strong>team score</strong> is the sum of your <strong>lowest <%= SCORES_THAT_COUNT %></strong> golfers' scores relative to par — the lower, the better.</li>
        <li>Your team needs at least <strong><%= MIN_CUT_MAKERS %></strong> golfers to make the cut to <strong>qualify</strong> for the team prize. Fewer than that and your team is <strong>DQ'd</strong> from the team prize (still eligible for the individual pot).</li>
        <li>The <strong>team prize</strong> goes to the qualified team with the lowest score. If two teams tie, whichever has the lowest single player score wins the tiebreak.</li>
        <li>The <strong>individual pot</strong> goes to whoever's single golfer scores lowest overall — no cut requirement.</li>
        <li>Scores update automatically from ESPN every 5 minutes once the tournament is underway.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Last Man Standing ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <h2 class="section-title mt-lg" id="last-man-standing">🏆 Last Man Standing</h2>
    <div class="card">
      <ol style="margin:0;padding-left:1.2rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.5rem">
        <li>Join a game before the host starts it. In the lobby, the host can add/remove players and set the entry fee per player.</li>
        <li>Each gameweek, pick <strong>one team</strong> — from the Premier League and/or Championship, depending on the game's settings — that you think will <strong>win</strong> their match.</li>
        <li>Picks lock at the kickoff of the gameweek's first match by default (the host can adjust the deadline). If you don't pick in time, you're <strong>automatically eliminated</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Win and you survive</strong> to the next week. A draw or a loss <strong>eliminates</strong> you.</li>
        <li>You can't pick the <strong>same team twice</strong> in the same round.</li>
        <li>The <strong>last player standing wins</strong> the prize pot (entry fee × number of players).</li>
        <li><strong>Rollover:</strong> if everyone gets eliminated in the same week, there's no winner — the prize <strong>doubles</strong> and the game restarts.</li>
        <li><strong>Auto-restart:</strong> once a round ends (win or rollover), the game automatically resets to week 1 and keeps going — nobody needs to re-register — until the host clicks <strong>Stop Game</strong>.</li>
        <li>Results are processed automatically once all of the gameweek's matches finish (the host can also process them manually at any time).</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Golf Scorecard ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <h2 class="section-title mt-lg" id="golf-scorecard">⛳ Golf Scorecard</h2>
    <div class="card">
      <ol style="margin:0;padding-left:1.2rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.5rem">
        <li>For a real round you're all playing together — enter everyone's strokes hole-by-hole as you go, or catch up afterwards. The host sets up the course (par and stroke index for all 18 holes) and picks a <strong>format</strong> when creating the game: <strong>Team</strong> or <strong>Individual</strong>.</li>
        <li>Scoring is <strong>net Stableford</strong>: 2 points for a net par on a hole, +1 for every shot better, −1 for every shot worse, floored at 0. Your handicap (set by the host in the lobby) determines how many strokes you receive on each hole based on its stroke index.</li>
        <li><strong>Team format:</strong> players join one of the host's teams from the lobby. Only a team's best <strong><%= TEAM_COUNTING_SCORES %></strong> Stableford scores count on each hole, so bigger teams aren't penalised for a weak link. The team with the most points wins.</li>
        <li><strong>Individual format:</strong> no teams — everyone just plays for their own net Stableford total. The player with the most points wins.</li>
        <li><strong>Tee times</strong> (team format only, optional): group players by who's actually playing together on the course. Anyone in a tee time can enter scores for the rest of their group, even across different teams — handy since usually only one person in the group is holding the scorecard. Individual-format games skip tee times entirely; you just enter your own scores.</li>
        <li>You can always enter your <strong>own</strong> scores yourself, whatever the format — the host/co-host can enter anyone's.</li>
        <li><strong>Closest to the pin</strong> can be enabled on any par-3 hole (the host chooses which). Whoever's nearest gets nominated by the host, or by anyone in that hole's tee time (team format) or any player (individual format) — nominating someone new replaces the previous holder.</li>
        <li>If there's an entry fee, the pot splits: <strong>team format</strong> is 50% winning team / 40% best individual net score / 10% nearest the pin. <strong>Individual format</strong> is 70% best individual net score / 30% nearest the pin (no team prize, since there are no teams).</li>
        <li>Once the host starts the game, teams and handicaps lock in — but tee times and closest-to-the-pin holes can still be changed at any point.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </main>

  <%- include('partials/footer') %>
</body>
</html>
